Ø'ûA declaration of a format is its type, its parser and its writer at once. Read, it turns bytes into a value whose fields are the pieces of its header; written, it turns that value back into the same bytes. DEFLATE packs its fields least significant bit first, reads its Huffman codes most significant bit first, and lets a copy reach back into what it has already written, even into the bytes it is writing. A stored block holds its bytes as they are; a fixed block uses the codes the format fixes; a dynamic block carries its own codes, written as the lengths of its codes, themselves written with a code of their own. A declaration of a format is its type, its parser and its writer at once. Read, it turns bytes into a value whose fields are the pieces of its header; written, it turns that value back into the same bytes. DEFLATE packs its fields least significant bit first, reads its Huffman codes most significant bit first, and lets a copy reach back into what it has already written, even into the bytes it is writing. A stored block holds its bytes as they are; a fixed block uses the codes the format fixes; a dynamic block carries its own codes, written as the lengths of its codes, themselves written with a code of their own. 